  "description": "<p><b>Type of Issue</b><br/>\nClarification / spec question \u2014 not a defect against the build.</p>\n\n<p><b>Context</b><br/>\nThe mobile \"All Filters\" bottom sheet has an <b>Apply Filters</b> button (batch apply). Desktop has no Apply button \u2014 each chip applies in real time. Need confirmation of the intended model and PRD documentation.</p>\n\n<p><b>Observed</b></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><b>Mobile:</b> combined \"All Filters\" sheet with a sticky <b>Apply Filters</b> button; selections apply on tap (batch). See screenshot.</li>\n\t<li><b>Desktop:</b> each filter is its own dropdown; selections apply live, no Apply button.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<p><b>What the PRD Says</b></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><b>S2-R6:</b> desktop filters in real time, no confirm/apply button.</li>\n\t<li><b>S12-R2:</b> mobile chips \"behave identically to desktop.\"</li>\n\t<li>\"Apply Filters\" / batch-apply appears <b>nowhere</b> in the PRD. The batch model exists only in the engineering implementation-decisions comment and the mobile test cases (C29622 / C29623 / C29624), not the ratified spec.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<p><b>Questions</b></p>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li>Is the intended model: mobile combined \"All Filters\" sheet = batch Apply, individual chips = real-time, desktop = real-time (S2-R6)?</li>\n\t<li>If yes, Story 12 should be updated to document the \"All Filters\" sheet and Apply button \u2014 S12-R2 currently says \"identical to desktop,\" which contradicts it.</li>\n\t<li>Confirm desktop is <b>not</b> getting an Apply button (stays real-time).</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<p><b>Reference</b></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>PRD: Filters v1.6 (<a href=\"https://shopview.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/shopviewapp/pages/572030978/Filters\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://shopview.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/shopviewapp/pages/572030978/Filters</a>) \u2014 S2-R6, S12-R2, \u00a74 Key Decisions; engineering implementation-decisions comment</li>\n\t<li>Test cases: C29622, C29623, C29624</li>\n</ul>\n",
